# A1/A1.2/A1_13_hobbies_and_free_time.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L4 (Part 1) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 4, Part 1)
# Source: PDF slide deck "L4 (Part 2) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 4, Part 2)
# Deck title: "4. Cours: Hobby a Fräizäit". Both parts merged and deduplicated by
# Luxembourgish form. Time-telling/weekday/frequency vocabulary is included
# because the deck teaches it specifically to let learners say when/how often
# they do their hobbies.

@lesson A1.13 "Hobbies & Free Time"

@word baken = to bake
@word schwammen = to swim
@word lafen = to run
@word sangen = to sing
@word lauschteren = to listen
@word héieren = to hear
@word kachen = to cook
@word molen = to draw
@word Gittar spillen = to play the guitar
@word Piano spillen = to play the piano
@word Fotoen maachen = to take photos
@word Timberen sammelen = to collect stamps
@word Vëlo fueren = to ride the bike
@word Fussball spillen = to play football
@word kucken = to look
@word ausgesinn = to look (appear)

@word relaxéieren = to relax
@word trainéieren = to train

@word ee Mol d'Woch = once a week
@word zwee Mol de Mount = twice a month
@word dräi Mol d'Joer = three times a year
@word all Dag = every day
@word oft = often
@word seelen = rarely
@word ni = never
@word normalerweis = normally

@word owes = in the evening
@word duerno = afterwards
@word dann = then
@word zu Mëtteg = at noon
@word heem = home

@word méindes = on Mondays
@word dënschdes = on Tuesdays
@word mëttwochs = on Wednesdays
@word donneschdes = on Thursdays
@word freides = on Fridays
@word samschdes = on Saturdays
@word sonndes = on Sundays
@word wiertes = on weekdays
@word de Weekend = the weekend

@word de Méindeg = Monday
@word de Freideg = Friday
@word de Samschdeg = Saturday
@word de Sonndeg = Sunday

@word typesch = typical
@word just = only
@word mech = me

@word d'Zeitung = the newspaper
@word d'Tëlee = the TV
@word de Liiblingsrestaurant = the favourite restaurant
@word d'Mëttegiessen = the lunch
@word Lëtzebuergesch = Luxembourgish
@word de Marathon = the marathon
@word d'Fräizäit = the free time
@word den Hobby = the hobby
@word de Partner = the partner
@word d'Kuchen = the cakes
@word d'Kanner = the children

@sentence
@lu Ech bake gär Kuchen.
@en I like baking cakes.
@distractor-en cook
@distractor-en read
@distractor-lu kachen
@distractor-lu liesen

@sentence
@lu Ech ginn zwee Mol d'Woch schwammen.
@en I go swimming twice a week.
@distractor-en run
@distractor-en month
@distractor-lu lafen
@distractor-lu Mount

@sentence
@lu Ech gi gär de Weekend spadséieren.
@en I like going for a walk at the weekend.
@distractor-en run
@distractor-en bake
@distractor-lu lafen
@distractor-lu baken

@sentence
@lu Ech lauschteren all Dag Musek.
@en I listen to music every day.
@distractor-en sometimes
@distractor-en sing
